WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.985
The CAG and the NHRC

2
00:00:01.985 --> 00:00:04.392
both watch the government.

3
00:00:04.392 --> 00:00:05.525
But one is in the

4
00:00:05.525 --> 00:00:07.928
Constitution, and one is not.

5
00:00:08.248 --> 00:00:10.641
Constitutional bodies are named in

6
00:00:10.641 --> 00:00:12.609
the Constitution itself.

7
00:00:12.609 --> 00:00:14.290
The Election Commission,

8
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:15.041
the U-P-S-C,

9
00:00:15.041 --> 00:00:16.632
the C-A-G and the Finance

10
00:00:16.632 --> 00:00:17.867
Commission.

11
00:00:18.222 --> 00:00:21.366
Statutory bodies come from ordinary

12
00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:23.489
laws, like the N-H-R-C,

13
00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:24.727
from 1993.

14
00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:26.716
Regulators like SEBI,

15
00:00:26.716 --> 00:00:27.789
from 1992,

16
00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:29.912
are statutory too.

17
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.890
A statutory body can be

18
00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.943
reshaped by a simple law.

19
00:00:33.943 --> 00:00:35.968
A constitutional one needs an

20
00:00:35.968 --> 00:00:38.797
amendment. That's real protection.

21
00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:40.776
Your turn.

22
00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:42.956
Which one is statutory?
